{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\nThe agentic plan-review engine (ADR 0123) signs a PASS for a run that read no code. `plan_review/agentic_verdict.py::adapt_findings` sets `coverage.llm_ran = True` and builds the verdict from the findings list alone. Nothing in `agentic.py`, `agentic_verdict.py` or the `agentic_review` step of `llm/workflow/gates/plan-review.yaml` checks how many tool calls the agent made. So an agent that answers `{\"findings\": []}` at once, with 0 `read_file`/`list_directory`/`search_files` calls, gets a non-blocking PASS and a certified plan-review attestation that the claim gate accepts.\n\nThe pipeline engine has no equivalent hole: every routed criterion chunk must return, and missing coverage resolves INDETERMINATE.\n\nThis is a silent-approval path in a gate.\n\n## Plan\nHow the count is available: a production agent call records the run shape on `result[\"_usage\"]` (`runner_support._merge_success_run_shape`, keys from `usage_log._SHAPE_FIELDS`, which include `tool_calls`), and the workflow recorder keeps each succeeded step's outputs, so the `agentic_review` step's `outputs._usage.tool_calls` is the number of tool calls the agent made. `gate_dispatch._consumed_diagnostic` already reads the same field.\n\n1. **RED first.** In `tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py`, add tests with a fake runner whose agentic answer carries `_usage`:\n   - `_usage = {\"tool_calls\": 0, \"requests\": 1}` with zero findings: the verdict is INDETERMINATE, `signature.signed` is False, `plan_review_status` is `unsigned`, `coverage.engine == \"agentic\"`, `coverage.resolution_class == \"FIX_AGENT_DESIGN\"`, and `coverage.diagnostic.tool_calls == 0`. Count attestations by reading `plan_review_status` before and after; no attestation is written.\n   - `_usage` present but with no `tool_calls` key (the shape reducer failed): also INDETERMINATE and unsigned (fail closed).\n   - `_usage = {\"tool_calls\": 3}` with zero findings: PASS and signed, as today.\n   - A fake runner that reports no `_usage` at all (the offline test runners): behavior unchanged, so every existing test keeps passing.\n   Confirm the first 2 fail before the fix.\n2. **Fix.** In `src/rebar/llm/workflow/plan_review_recovery.py`, add `agentic_unread_error(rec) -> BaseException | None`: it finds the succeeded `agentic_review` step record; when its `outputs._usage` is a dict whose `tool_calls` is missing or 0, it returns an `LLMRunnerError(\"agentic review made no tool calls: it read no code\")` carrying an `LLMOutcome(FIX_AGENT_DESIGN, sanitized diagnostic with tool_calls and requests, retryable=False)`; otherwise `None`.\n3. In `gate_dispatch` (plan-review success branch, before returning the terminal verdict): when `engine == \"agentic\"` and `agentic_unread_error(rec)` returns an error, return `_degraded_plan_review_verdict(ctx, cfg, error=..., ...)`, the same path every other failed agentic run takes, so the verdict is an unsigned INDETERMINATE with `resolution_class` and diagnostic on coverage. A floor-blocked or not-claimable review never runs `agentic_review`, so it is unaffected.\n4. ADR 0123 section 3 (\"Severity-to-verdict mapping\"): add that an agentic run with zero tool calls resolves INDETERMINATE (FIX_AGENT_DESIGN) and is never signed.\n\nBehavior is unconditional: no config key, env var or flag.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] An agentic run that made 0 tool calls (or whose tool-call count is missing from a reported `_usage`) resolves INDETERMINATE through the existing degraded-verdict path, with `resolution_class` FIX_AGENT_DESIGN and the tool-call count on `coverage.diagnostic`, and mints no attestation, pinned by tests.\n- [ ] An agentic run with at least 1 tool call still PASSes and signs, pinned by a test.\n- [ ] ADR 0123 states the zero-tool-call rule.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794565010736775001,"uuid":"276db621-40f4-4e72-8814-6018b0180589"}